From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:13:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Fix loop bound in uncertainty maximum

The loop iterated while i < Eigen::Dynamic, which is -1, so the loop
body never ran and uncertaintyMaximum() always returned 1.0. Iterate
over the opinion's dimensions instead and skip states with a zero base
rate, which do not constrain the maximum uncertainty.
---
 src/MultinomialOpinion.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/MultinomialOpinion.cpp b/src/MultinomialOpinion.cpp
index b3b1723..a5288ad 100644
--- a/src/MultinomialOpinion.cpp
+++ b/src/MultinomialOpinion.cpp
@@ -390,8 +390,13 @@ double MultinomialOpinion::uncertaintyMaximum() const
   double min_u                 = 1.0;
   MultinomialOpinion::Vector p = projectionMat();
 
-  for (int i = 0; i < Eigen::Dynamic; ++i)
+  for (Eigen::Index i = 0; i < m_dim; ++i)
   {
+    // States without base rate do not constrain the uncertainty
+    if (m_base_rate(i) <= 0.0)
+    {
+      continue;
+    }
     double u = p(i) / m_base_rate(i);
     if (u < min_u)
     {
